{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/283222-can-a-mummy-be-contacted-when-sleeping","id":283222,"title":"Can a Mummy be contacted when sleeping?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-15T21:39:15-07:00","id":283222,"title":"Can a Mummy be contacted when sleeping?","content":"When a Mummy is between cycles or awakenings, is it possible for them to be contacted? In dreams or even a mage using Arcana to contact them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T21:48:40-07:00","id":283237,"title":"","content":"I'd usually say no. When they're resting in henet, their consciousness appears to be in Duat. Given the presence of a mystic barrier preventing Mummies from remembering anything that happens in Duat, they certainly wouldn't remember any such communication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T22:36:47-07:00","id":283402,"title":"","content":"A mummy in henet is a mummy being dead. The only way to make him talk to you is waking him up, I'd say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T05:48:31-07:00","id":283764,"title":"","content":"Isn't there an Utterance that allows something like this? Dreams of Dead Gods or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T06:08:37-07:00","id":283775,"title":"","content":"It can be used by a Mummy in henet, to inflict dreams on the mortal world. It doesn't let the Mummy receive messages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T09:52:58-07:00","id":285083,"title":"","content":"I would say no.<br /> <br /> When not in the Descent, the mummy is kind of dreaming in a way, but still &quot;awake&quot; in other ways - her soul is in henet, doing whatever it is one does in hemet when not just in a death cycle. Henet isn't accessible by anyone who isn't a Mummy, it seems, and it may also be that each Mummy is in their own henet - that is, two Mummies in henet at the same time will never run into each other (or maybe they will, but they'll never remember it).<br /> <br /> I would treat the repose of henet as a totally inviolate place where the Mummy's soul can never be reached or contacted by any entity aside from the Judges or Anpu, save for the mechanism of the Call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T10:01:15-07:00","id":285093,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I had an idea that a Tremere Lich was the lover to a Mummy and they contacted each other while he was in henet. Does anyone have any workaround ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T14:01:34-07:00","id":285312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/283222-can-a-mummy-be-contacted-when-sleeping?p=285093#post285093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have any workaround ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're in solid house-rule territory here, so I'd say do whatever makes sense for your story and your table. But it should be pretty epic and probably have a degree of backlash for a mortal thing, even a vampire, to contact henet in any way. Vampires aren't immune to Jar of Teeth, after all. <br /> <br /> I don't know if Dreams of Dead Gods would work on vampires, but maybe. Barring that the only official thing would be for the vampire to get some control over the Mummy's cult and demand they raise him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T14:49:22-07:00","id":285427,"title":"","content":"If you haven't read the ST section, it should at least hint that Mummies arent exactly asleep like torpor. Their souls are very busy during henet, due to the Judges. If I allowed it, itd have to be more like temporarily reaching out to summon a part of their soul. Id make it space 3 + 5 in the subtle arcana of the pillar of choice (mind for ab, death for sheut, etc) to summon as a ghostly apparition from duat. The mummy couldnt describe henet or duat, and may not remember the communication when it rises, but itd work in a pinch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T16:43:52-07:00","id":285494,"title":"","content":"I think a Mummy in henet should be left alone. That's the whole risk of being a cultist: do I really dare to call the Mummy from its death state just to ask it a couple questions? Do I really dare temporarily drain a relic, try to burn its sleeping corpse, or convince its sadikh to sacrifice itself just to communicate with it?<br /> <br /> That's how plots happen. A Mummy wakes up and finds out that all the guidelines they left for their cult <i>haven't</i> been followed, and now they have to set things back in order. If they could just communicate in henet then everything would be fine, right?<br /> <br /> I might allow a 'mortal sorcerer' a powerful spell which lets them glimpse the Mummy's soul in Duat which, effectively, is like the old (and new?) Common Sense merit where you ask the GM some questions for hints, but this would come as a breaking point for the sorcerer or, at least, it would trigger Sybaris in him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T18:01:22-07:00","id":285575,"title":"","content":"Well, the thing I was thinking about was to have the Mage be able to influence the cult to bring the mummy back on out when she needs him or when she wishes to let him know that his plans have come to fruition and what his new ones are. So forth and so on. Not just on a whim. And this time, his plans get interrupted by the players as all great villains plans do. And all ST plans for that matter now that I think about it....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}